{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>In the very midst of that day Avraham was circumcised, etc.</b> Even though it was already stated, ״וַיָּמָל בְּשַׂר עָרְלָתָם״ (Genesis 17:23), and it is written, ״בְּהִמּוֹלוֹ אֵת בְּשַׂר עָרְלָתוֹ״ (Genesis 17:25), nevertheless Scripture returned and specified to say that he performed even his own circumcision in the very midst of that day, in the view of all, and he was not embarrassed before those who looked on. For according to Rashi's explanation it is difficult — why should the scorners of the generation have sought to mock him? And according to the midrash of our Sages of blessed memory (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 29), he was circumcised on Yom HaKippurim, as they derived from a gezerah shavah of ״בְּעֶצֶם הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The syntactic transition at 'ולמדרש רבותינו' is elliptical: the Kli Yakar notes that according to the midrash assigning the circumcision to Yom Kippur, the phrase 'בעצם היום הזה' finds its full resonance, leaving the question about the scorners applicable principally to Rashi's reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:30.775033624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}